Small: about seven lines in one file. In src/components/LookUp.tsx, close the dialog on a change of route with an effect in LookUp:

import { useLocation } from 'react-router-dom';
...
const { pathname } = useLocation();
useEffect(() => { if (ref.current?.open) ref.current.close(); }, [pathname]);

LookUp is a child of Shell, so in the same commit its effect runs before the route effect of Shell. The modal is gone when focusViewHeading runs, so focus lands on the new heading (C7). The close event that comes later still clears the request through onClose, as it does today. I tested this as described in the evidence.

Small, in one file, src/components/LookUp.tsx: close the dialog on a change of route. LookUp is a child of Shell, so its effect runs before the shell's route effect, and the C7 move to the new h2 then works:

import { useLocation } from 'react-router-dom';
...
const { pathname } = useLocation();
useEffect(() => { if (ref.current?.open) ref.current.close(); }, [pathname]);

The close event that follows clears the request through closeLookUp, and onClose leaves focus on the new heading. I tested this on a scratch build: focus goes to "Your path", Escape without Back still returns to the opener, and the smoke gate passes 22 of 22. A browser Back that closes only the dialog and keeps the session would need a history entry for the dialog. That is a design change C1 and U-17 do not ask for, and a Back with no dialog open also ends the session.

Small, in src/App.tsx only. Keep the registration from onRegisteredSW in a ref (reg.current = registration). Then change reload() as below:

  asked.current = true;
  const waiting = reg.current?.waiting ?? null;
  if (takenOver.current || !waiting) { window.location.reload(); return; }
  if (!navigator.serviceWorker.controller) waiting.addEventListener('statechange', () => { if (waiting.state === 'activated') window.location.reload(); });
  void updateServiceWorker(true);

When no worker waits, the new worker is already active, so a plain reload loads the new version. When a worker waits but none controls the page, the page reloads once that worker is activated. I tested this in a scratch build: the first-visit, controlled and two-copy cases all reload on build 2.

Also fix the comment at App.tsx:65. Smoke case 16 tests only a controlled page; a first-visit step there would catch a return of this defect.

Add one effect to Shell in src/App.tsx, after the route effect. It moves focus to the heading of the open dialog, or of the view, when a retry has loaded the library and focus has fallen to the body:

  const { content } = useApp();
  const lastContent = useRef(content);
  useEffect(() => {
    const before = lastContent.current;
    lastContent.current = content;
    if (!before || before === content || document.activeElement !== document.body) return;
    const place = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('dialog[open]') ?? mainRef.current;
    if (place) return focusViewHeading(place);
  }, [content]);

- At the first load `before` is null, so C7's rule of no focus move at the first load holds.
- A failed retry keeps its button, so focus is not on the body and nothing moves.
- One effect covers all five places: the shell, the Drill, Reference, the Radio test and the look-up dialog.

The fix is small: about 10 lines in one file. LookUp.tsx needs no change. I tested it on a scratch build.
